         <p>
            <lb/>Cover Text</p>
         <head>THE GREAT PANJANDRUM<lb/>HIMSELF</head>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>So she went into the garden to cut a cabbage-leaf</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>to make</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>an apple-pie;</p>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>and at the same time a great she-bear,<lb/>coming down the street, pops its head<lb/>into the shop.</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>What! no soap?</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>So he died,</p>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>and she very imprudently married the Barber:</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>and there were present</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>the Picninnies, and the Joblillies,</p>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>and the Garyulies,</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>and the great Panjandrum himself, with<lb/>the little round button at top;</p>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>and they all fell to playing the game of<lb/>catch-as-catch-can,</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>till the gunpowder ran out at the heels<lb/>of their boots.</p>
         <p>watercolor painting</p>
         <p>line drawing</p>
         <p>back cover</p>
